"P3376091772" "Samuel O'Reilly"
// ProfessionString :
// DescriptionString :
"P1018955156" "Samuel O'Reilly is a fill-in for the original instructor who had to make a quick departure.  (The university wishes him well on all his future endeavors and hopes they'll commute his sentence in no time)  Mr. O'Reilly took the job because he liked the lab coat.  He does not really have experience in Engineering or Laboratory work, but he can regurgitate course materials with ease."
// ContactRequiresText :
// FirstVisitString :
"P493743975" "Well hello!  I'm Samuel O'Reilly, your instructor!  I teach the Workbench and Results class!  I am an instructor, which is why I wear this very important looking labcoat.  You probably thought I was a doctor.  It happens all the time.  I have that sharp contemplative look about me."
// HelloString :
"P774213866" "And hello again, fine student!  Yes, the labcoat is still a wonder, is it not?  It's the perfect accessory for my Workbench and Results instruction.  Feel free to browse the computer if you missed anything I taught you."
// IDontKnowYouString :
"P4197169987" "Are you in this class?  Hm.  I do not see you on my list.  You were drawn to my spectacular labcoat weren't you?  I suspected as much.  <br><br>Well, I'm afraid you'll need to enroll for the Program first.  Go see Dean Yu.  He will get you started."
// NoTasksRemainingString :
"P608906163" "You really should go see {LastContactName} now, {VillainName}. I was quite flattering when I told him to expect you."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToFriend :
// LocationString :
// IntroString :
"P305516507" "This course is a brief overview of the how Workbenches function as well as all the different kinds of items (not just Enhancements) that you can create using the Workbenches.<br><br>Samuel O'Reilly is located on the second floor of the Laboratory."
// IntroAcceptString :
// IntroSendoffString :
"P3354611791" "The next class is about Workbenches and Results taught by:"
// IntroduceOneContact :
"P1308315151" "Fine work, student.  Fine work!  Perhaps one day you'll wear a labcoat just like mine.  Off you go to your next class."
